{"name":"Sandy Hair","hex":"#b7ac97","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sandy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with sand.","Sprinkled with sand."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sandwich","Ellipsis of pecan sandy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandy"},{"term":"hair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigmented filament of keratin which grows from a follicle on the skin of humans and other mammals.","The collection or mass of such growths growing from the skin of humans and animals, and forming a covering for any part or the whole body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the hair from.","To grow hair (where there was a bald spot)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alex Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Alexander Hair was a Scottish footballer who played as a centre forward."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Hair","wikidata":"Q4717112"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair","wikidata":"Q28472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg/500px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_8115_Human_hair_and_Merino_wool_fibre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikim